\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Mean slice size by circuit width, for RQ1. The grey bars are the dependence set, the smallest size a dependence-complete slice can have. Corpus~L has no grey bar, because its ground truth would need exact simulation of every perturbation at 15 to 20 qubits. Commutation is shown where Qiskit's pass applies.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:size}{{4}{10}{}{figure.4}{}}
